  "term": "epileptiform seizure",
  "definition": "In this historical source, an epileptiform seizure is a seizure resembling epilepsy, ranging from brief pallor, confusion, or small muscle twitches to major convulsive attacks. Consciousness may be partly or fully lost, and the attack is often followed by temporary weakness or paralysis in the affected parts.",
